{
  "scenarioVersion": 2,
  "meta": {
    "name": "Adjacent-lane incursion authored the way an author actually writes it",
    "description": "The capability this proves is not \"a multi-lane corridor exists\" \u2014 22.9% of map-intel Segments across all five dev maps already have minThroughLanesSameDir >= 2. It is that an actor authored INTO the adjacent lane now truthfully lands there. `neighbour` is written the obvious way, `kind: \"on_reference\"` with `pose.laneOffset: -1`, which is what an author reaches for when told \"start in the lane beside the ego\". Until now the adapter discarded `pose.laneOffset` for that kind, the matcher bound k = 0, and the car spawned inside the ego and sat there \u2014 with no note, no warning, and `template validate` reporting ok. The offset is now carried into a `lane_offset` binding resolved with `onMissing: \"fail\"`, so this template either gets a genuinely adjacent car or rejects the site. The corridor clause `throughLanesSameDir >= 2` is what makes the second outcome rare rather than the rule. The `parked-run` prop row is authored in the same adjacent lane and proves the same fix on the prop path, which resolves through `framePosePoint` rather than through the matcher.",
    "createdAt": "2026-08-07T00:00:00.000Z",
    "modifiedAt": "2026-08-07T00:00:00.000Z",
    "appVersion": "uniscenarios/0.0.1",
    "archetype": "C2.adjacent-lane-incursion",
    "tags": [
      "multilane",
      "cut-in",
      "lane-offset",
      "caps-map"
    ],
